{%- comment -%}
  Turn any asset or image URL into an absolute one, for structured data.

  schema.org needs absolute URLs; a relative one silently invalidates the rich
  result. The three shapes that reach this are all handled:

    //cdn.shopify.com/...   what image_url and asset_url return on Shopify
    https://...             already absolute, left alone
    /assets/...             root-relative, as in a local render

  Blindly prepending "https:" — the common shortcut — turns the third shape into
  "https:/assets/..." and the second into "https:https://...".

  Usage:
    {%- capture img -%}{%- render 'absolute-url', src: some_url -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  Accepts: src (required), base (optional, defaults to the shop URL)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign root = base | default: shop.secure_url | default: shop.url
  assign head = src | slice: 0, 2
  if head == '//'
    echo src | prepend: 'https:'
  elsif head == 'ht'
    echo src
  else
    echo src | prepend: root
  endif
-%}
